Aircraft cover (DCS Control, 2026-11-26): [ofxr] dcs_motion_cover, the fix the fg-diag live diagnosis found, plus the
focus-MV review's HIGH-1 and LOW-3.
- Diagnosis (artifacts/motion-study/fg-diag, docs/FOCUS_MOTION.md): DCS's MVs of the AI aircraft are right, but its
  class lands on the MV texels' centres for only 15-46 % of what is drawn of it at 450-1800 m; the rest reads as the
  sky with the sky's vector, the gather stays on that class, the scatter wins 4-20 %, and the colour check passes the
  sky's vector because a faint aircraft differs from the sky by less than 16/255: the generated frame is about 0.9 of a
  cross-fade of the aircraft's two places.
- Lever 1 (dcs_motion.hlsl, resample Flags bit 2): a cell whose nearest texel is the sky takes the vector and class of
  the model texel (DCS's model class) among the eight around it nearest the sample point; in the focus view with its
  depth plane a farther surface gives way too, to the nearest model texel by depth. A covered cell is an edge cell, so
  the scatter carries it. Periphery and focus resample (fine grid included).
- Lever 2: DcsMotionNearCS, after the scatter, sets bit 31 of both outputs' scatter keys on a sky cell with a model cell
  within about 16 output px (the scatter's keys never reach bit 31; the composition masks it). frame_synthesis.hlsl
  quality_cover_sky: a sky gather with that bit whose two samples differ at all (encoded, > 2/255) and where the two
  frames do not agree at the very pixel (> 2/255: HUD strokes stay put) first tries the aircraft's own vector (the
  current end and rings 1-3 cells out, dcs_motion_sky_occlusion's fixed-point test); where none holds but a surface was
  seen, the frame whose end DCS's class map calls sky alone. Before dcs_motion_sky_occlusion, which stays as it was.
- The key is a quality key (implicit_layer::kFgQualityKeys bit 16, shader bit 21: live). With it the only key on, a pair
  binds a "_cover" twin of the compositions with DCS's MVs (XRFG_FG_COVER_ONLY=1: the cover's code alone, the other
  options and the diagnosis records compiled out: the plain composition's 27-28 registers, where the _extras twin has 34
  and costs 3X about 0.6 ms at 5424 px); built in the same background build as the _extras twins. With other keys on,
  the _extras twin (which has the cover too). Off: no
  dispatch, no bit, every composition as before (output hashes of XRFG_TEST_DCS_MOTION and XRFG_TEST_FG_FOCUS_MOTION
  equal to 0129's).
- Review HIGH-1 (0128): an eye's focus MVs are used only where the pair's previous frame has that eye's focus record
  too and its fovTan moved by at most 1.5 focus texels (the DLSS jitter moves the jittered fovTan by 0.5-1 texel every
  frame; gate P1 live: with the gaze still DCS's focus MVs match the CURRENT fovTan at both ends, residual 0.000 px
  against the periphery's MVs, so the residual keeps the current fovTan; focus_prev_fov, DcsMotionParameters 48 DWORDs,
  stays zero). Else the periphery's MVs cover the focus region, as without dcs_motion_focus. Counted: CockpitMaskPairCounters::motion_focus_moved, cockpit_mask result=12 c bits 16-31.
- Review LOW-3: the focus import checks the jitters are finite, as the periphery's.
- 0129's diagnosis records are 16 bytes (json recordStride): word 2 the vector composed along (f16 x, y), word 3 bit 0
  dcs_motion_cover's aircraft vector, bit 1 its one-frame rule, bit 2 the reach bit.
- tests/fg_cover.inc (XRFG_TEST_FG_COVER, ctest xrfg_d3d12_fg_cover, NVIDIA hardware): M0b small aircraft (4-8 px, a
  2 px light), crossings at 450-1800 m (day, dusk), the F2 orbit, HUD over the sky, wires, smoke; flow / off / cover /
  sky / sky+cover / d2 off / d2 cover; per region MAE, cross-fade fraction, the share of aircraft pixels composed as
  along the true motion to within 1 px; gates: HUD, smoke, lights, wires, far and the image not worse with the key, no
  change without MVs, the crossings' cross-fade fraction down. XRFG_TEST_DCS_MOTION_BENCH_SKY=1: the bench's world is
  the sky.
- Live round 2 (fg-cover, 2026-11-26): the cover's reach is two MV texels (kCoverReach), and lever 2's fixed point
  counts when it lands within two cells of a cell of the candidate's class and vector, where the two frames' samples
  agree (live 99.97 % of the aircraft candidates' fixed points fell on cells DCS calls sky, 65 % within two cells of the
  aircraft). tests/fg_cover.inc XRFG_TEST_FG_COVER_LIVE=<dir>: live pairs exported from a flight's dumps
  (export_live_fixture.py): the frame's MV / class atlases, the real frames in target pixels, the measured motion.

